# GCU400 reflection_pad1d strategy (2026-11-16 perf rewrite, ported from the
# reflection_pad2d / _pad_circular row-group family): the previous kernel
# launched grid=(B, cdiv(W_out, 1024)) with a per-lane abs/%/where reflection
# chain, so the big bench shape paid 6144 programs on the ~52ns/program
# dispatch floor (~324us measured, dtype-independent) and narrow shapes issued
# mostly-masked 1024-lane blocks. The rewrite keeps one kernel launch and
# decomposes the op along output rows (for 1d every row is an affine interior
# copy - there is no height reflection):
#   * phase 1 (bulk): U-row affine groups; all U contiguous row loads are
#     issued before the U contiguous stores to hide the ~450ns load latency.
#     Partial tail rows (R % U) run as their own one-row-per-iteration
#     grid-strided loop so small-R shapes stay parallel instead of paying a
#     serial clamped chain.
#   * phase 2 (pads): the left/right mirror lanes (pl+pr per row, a few
#     percent of the output) are copied by a per-lane gather loop, so bulk
#     programs never issue tiny ops.
# Grid is capped at 48 (one program per SPC); rows/lanes are grid-strided.
# Wide rows (W > 8192) take a chunked general path; row spaces whose flat
# element offsets reach 2^31 take the WIDE int64 fallback for correctness.


